# Dev — toolchains and command line tools.
#
# Neovim installs its language servers through Mason, which needs the runtimes
# below to be present: rust-analyzer comes from rustup, gopls from go, and the
# JavaScript servers from node (already in core, since the editor is core).

# ── Toolchains ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
go
rustup                      # manages the toolchain; run `rustup default stable`
clang                       # C/C++ compiler and clangd
uv                          # Python environments and tools
pnpm
bun
luarocks                    # Lua rocks, used by a few Neovim plugins
tree-sitter-cli             # nvim-treesitter builds parsers with it

# ── Containers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
docker
docker-buildx
docker-compose

# ── Command line ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tmux
fzf
openssh
sshpass
openbsd-netcat
lazysql                     # database TUI — AUR
supabase-bin                # Supabase CLI — AUR
